# Code owners for Loki. Listed owners are auto-requested for review on matching paths.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# Every rule here names the same person, so nothing below changes WHO reviews. What it
# changes is the review being requested automatically and, if the branch ruleset turns
# on "Require review from Code Owners", being required. The paths are listed
# separately from the catch-all so that the reason each one is sensitive stays written
# down, and so a second maintainer can be added to one line without inheriting all of
# them.
#
# Last match wins in this file — later rules override earlier ones, which is the
# opposite of .gitignore. The catch-all therefore has to come first.

# Default owner for everything in the repository.
*                       @trinadhthatakula

# Release-gating and CI configuration. A change here can alter what every other pull
# request is allowed to merge, or what gets published to users, without touching a
# line of app code.
/.github/               @trinadhthatakula
/gradle.properties      @trinadhthatakula
/release-notes/         @trinadhthatakula
/.coderabbit.yaml       @trinadhthatakula

# The privileged surface. These files reach android.permission.READ_LOGS through a
# root shell or through Shizuku's binder, so code here runs with authority the app
# itself does not have — and a command assembled from an untrusted string is a shell
# injection into that authority. See CONTRIBUTING.md and .github/SECURITY.md.
/app/src/main/java/com/valhalla/loki/model/SuCli.kt              @trinadhthatakula
/app/src/main/java/com/valhalla/loki/model/PermissionManager.kt   @trinadhthatakula
/app/src/main/java/com/valhalla/loki/services/                    @trinadhthatakula
/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml                                 @trinadhthatakula

# Signing and shrinking. proguard-rules.pro decides what survives R8 in the APK that
# ships, and app/build.gradle.kts holds the signing config and the version derivation.
/app/build.gradle.kts   @trinadhthatakula
/app/proguard-rules.pro @trinadhthatakula
